@startuml
state program #pink
program : on chain account program

state wallet #yellow
wallet : payer wallet interaction

state screen #cyan
screen : visible or interactive content

state identified <<choice>>
state sign_up #cyan
state create_account
state find_contract
state authorize #yellow
state open_contract #pink
state metered_page #cyan
state meter_and_settle #pink
state check_limit <<choice>>
state account_page #cyan
state renew_contract #pink
state close_contract #pink

[*] -[bold]-> identified : navigate
identified --> sign_up : viewer not identified
identified -[bold]-> find_contract : viewer's wallet address known

find_contract : derive the contract address from site and wallet address
find_contract : read the account
find_contract -> sign_up : no contract
find_contract -[bold]-> check_limit : contract found

sign_up : inform cost per fetch
sign_up : prompt limit amount
sign_up : enforce minimum on limit amount
sign_up --> create_account : sign up

create_account : enforce minimum on limit amount
create_account : limit amount
create_account : zero paid amount
create_account : zero used amount
create_account --> authorize

authorize : payer wallet authorizes spending up to the limit
authorize : reused for both initial sign-up and limit renewal
authorize -> sign_up : wallet cancelled (sign-up)
authorize --> open_contract : wallet signed (sign-up)
authorize -> account_page : wallet cancelled (renewal)
authorize -[bold]-> [*] : wallet signed (renewal), navigate

open_contract : create the contract for this site and payer
open_contract --> check_limit

metered_page : display metered content as navigated
metered_page -[bold]-> [*] : navigate

meter_and_settle : bump used amount on account by page increment
meter_and_settle : if unpaid balance crosses collection threshold,
meter_and_settle : transfer the entire unpaid balance in same instruction
meter_and_settle : increment and transfer succeed or fail together (atomic)
meter_and_settle -[bold]-> metered_page : instruction succeeded
meter_and_settle --> account_page : instruction failed (insufficient funds)

check_limit -> account_page : limit reached
check_limit -[bold]-> meter_and_settle : meter below limit

account_page: show current limit, cost per page
account_page: show used and paid amount
account_page: to change wallets, delete the account and sign-up with the new wallet
account_page: prompt new limit for renewal
account_page: enforce minimum on limit amount
account_page -> [*] : navigate
account_page --> renew_contract : renew
account_page --> close_contract : delete

renew_contract: enforce minimum on limit amount
renew_contract: reduce used amount by paid amount
renew_contract: zero paid amount
renew_contract: set new limit amount
renew_contract --> authorize : re-authorize new limit

close_contract : meter_and_settle takes the entire unpaid balance,
close_contract : so residue is always below the collection threshold
close_contract : leave the residue uncollected (take the loss)
close_contract --> [*] : navigate

legend left
Colour says what kind of step it is, not who runs it.
The pink (on chain) steps divide by signer:
  payer signs .......... open_contract, renew_contract, close_contract
  site authority signs . meter_and_settle
Identifying the viewer is the integrator's own business. This diagram assumes
only that the site can map the viewer to a wallet address; see
wasm-client/SPEC.md section 4.
endlegend

@enduml
